lated 41,000 items last year. It also hosted 312 public programs, provided 9,400 sessions on its public computers, and served as a designated cooling center on eleven days."}]]}],["$","p","1",{"className":"flex gap-3","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"w-5 shrink-0 pt-1 text-right text-sm font-semibold tabular-nums text-eng-navy-300","aria-hidden":"true","children":2}],["$","span",null,{"children":"City budget discussions still describe library funding as spending on books. That description is decades out of date, and it quietly makes the case for cuts. If a library is a book warehouse, then a city with declining print circulation has an obvious place to save money."}]]}],["$","p","2",{"className":"flex gap-3","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"w-5 shrink-0 pt-1 text-right text-sm font-semibold tabular-nums text-eng-navy-300","aria-hidden":"true","children":3}],["$","span",null,{"children":"But the computer sessions are not incidental. For a resident applying for a job, renewing a benefit, or filing a form that no longer exists on paper, the branch is often the only free place to sit down with a keyboard and get help using it."}]]}],["$","p","3",{"className":"flex gap-3","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"w-5 shrink-0 pt-1 text-right text-sm font-semibold tabular-nums text-eng-navy-300","aria-hidden":"true","children":4}],["$","span",null,{"children":"I do not think the library should be exempt from budget scrutiny. Every department should have to justify what it costs. I think the justification should be measured against what the library actually does, and the current accounting does not measure that at all."}]]}]]}],"$undefined",["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-5 border-t border-eng-navy-100 pt-3 text-xs italic text-eng-navy-400","children":"Original passage — BEOC Academic Bridge"}]]}]]}]],["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-4","children":["$L29","$L2a","$L2b"]}]]}]]}]
